%% DM26-0670

%% A client subscribes to a topic. The path is the code as built (2026-10-21, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md);
%% the decision at the Listener is the design (docs/architecture/policy-enforcement.md, stage 5), not built yet.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (TcpClientActor)
    participant Listener
    participant Policy as Broker's PolicyLookup<br/>(designed)
    participant Session as SessionAgent
    participant Broker
    participant Topics as TopicManager / TopicAgent
    participant Subs as SubscriberManager / SubscriberAgent

    Note over Client,Listener: the connection's identity is the leaf certificate's first DNS SAN,<br/>taken at the handshake, and the leaf is kept (designed) for its p: names
    Client->>Listener: SubscribeRequest(registration_id, topic)
    alt not registered, or another session's id
        Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Err "not registered")
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Listener,Policy: DESIGNED: the decision, before anything is created
    Listener->>Policy: subscribe, Topic::"topic", Identity::"identity",<br/>facts: workload, declared or implied
    alt policy loaded and it speaks
        Policy-->>Listener: Allow or Deny (Cedar overrides the certificate, both ways)
    else no policy, or it does not speak
        Listener->>Listener: the floor: implied topics from the identity,<br/>declared topics from the certificate's p:sub: names
    end
    alt refused (default deny)
        Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Err "refused: ...")
        Note right of Client: ClientEvent::SubscribeRefused (stage 0), the agent logs it
    end
    end

    Listener->>Session: SubscribeRequest(topic)
    Session->>Broker: SubscribeRequest(registration_id, topic)
    Broker->>Topics: ensure_topic_and_subscribe (a topic is created on first use)
    Topics->>Subs: CreateSubscriber(registration_id:topic)
    Subs-->>Topics: SubscriberAgent
    Topics->>Topics: TopicAgent AddSubscriber, deliver any queued messages
    Listener-->>Client: SubscribeAcknowledgment(Ok) (designed: today a success is not acknowledged)
